  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1135 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nSfc low advances eastward into the central Plains on Saturday with\nthe corresponding pressure gradient and mixing of the early day\nlow level jet leading to stronger winds. Near record temperatures\nand drier dewpoints will also be in place resulting in a broader\nregion of heightened fire weather concerns for Saturday afternoon.\nOngoing drought conditions will for rapid fire spread in both\ngrassland and larger timber fuels. Remain aware of ongoing county\nlevel burn bans.\n\nStorms will develop west of the local region by Saturday evening\nand spread eastward into early Sunday morning. The eastward\nadvance of the precip will stall by Sunday morning before the\nactual cold front marks another uptick in shower and storm\ncoverage by Sunday afternoon and evening spreading eastward\nthrough early Monday. \n\nA period of post frontal cloudiness and rain chances may persist\ninto Monday with cooler sfc high pressure building southward and\npersisting across the region through much of next week. This will\nmark a notable cool down with readings much more typical of late\nSeptember.",
